**major** — `filter_excluded` uses a mutable default `excluded=[]` and appends into it. Later calls return paths from earlier calls, so the exclusion set grows and is wrong.

**major** — `copy_many` treats every `copy_file` return as success. `copy_file` swallows `OSError` after `open(dst, "wb")` truncates the destination, so a missing source or a failed write is reported in `done`. Callers will not retry, and the previous destination contents can be lost.

**major** — `merge_manifest` keeps the old entry when `old["mtime"] > new["mtime"]`. A source update with an older timestamp (restore, clock skew, `cp -p`) is dropped, so the merged manifest no longer matches the source. Paths absent from `new_manifest` are never removed.

**minor** — `merge_manifest` never writes `dst_manifest_path`. The docstring says it merges into the destination manifest, but the on-disk file is left unchanged unless the caller persists the return value.
